      "body": "Supersedes #41628, which was closed for inactivity.\n\n## Motivation\n\nUpstream now covers the original PR's larger-row norm/quantization fusions, scale-row addressing, scale padding and query RoPE/store fusion. The remaining change is extending the existing Blackwell decode/verification paths through 1,024 rows.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Extend the CUDA target-verification `wo_a` path and HC post-split dispatch through 1,024 rows.\n- Extend the fused MoE all-reduce dispatch and deferred-output-shape range through 1,024 rows, retaining push-slot and counter capacity checks.\n- Give DeepSeek-V4.1 TP4 a dedicated 12 MiB push slot and 1,024 counters. Its two slots across four ranks use 96 MiB per rank; other layouts retain their existing communicator capacity.\n\nNo CUDA kernels or arithmetic are changed. Superseded norm and RoPE implementations are omitted in favor of current upstream.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe remaining limits and TP4 workspace sizes match the original PR. Python syntax and undefined-name checks pass. No full suite or GPU validation was rerun after the upstream merge.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40987477274](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40987477274)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40987477130](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40987477130)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40987477220](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40987477220)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
